#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fleet-jobs — pane-scoped durable jobs for builds, the fleet suite, and render-verify.

A job outlives the tool call, Claude invocation, or Codex session that started
it: a new-session supervisor owns the child, appends its output to a durable
log, and publishes the terminal status. A later invocation reads, waits for,
or cancels the same job without ps, pgrep, or a PID-addressed kill.

Usage:
  fleet-jobs start build [--name NAME] -- <ir-build arguments>
  fleet-jobs start fleet-tests [--name NAME] [--only <substring>]
  fleet-jobs start render-verify [--name NAME] -- <render-verify arguments>
  fleet-jobs status [--json] <job-id>
  fleet-jobs wait [--quiet] [--timeout SECONDS] <job-id>
  fleet-jobs kill <job-id>
  fleet-jobs list [--json]

Profiles are fixed; there is no executable, path, or shell-string form.
  build          the ir-build adjacent to this script (fleet-build --detach
                 enters here after its format -> format-changed rewrite)
  fleet-tests    <cwd's checkout>/scripts/fleet/tests/run_all.sh
  render-verify  <cwd's checkout>/scripts/render-verify.py; --build-dir,
                 --update-references and --force are rejected, a pane
                 runs one render-verify job at a time, and the log opens
                 with the displays the job's session can reach

wait streams the job log and exits with the child's exit code; a job that is
still running when --timeout elapses exits 124, a lost job exits 1, and a
job with a process that outlived the supervisor's SIGKILL fails with 125. The
last stderr line always names the job's state.

State: ${FLEET_STATE_DIR:-~/.fleet/state}/jobs/<pane>/<job-id>/{meta.json,job.log}.
The pane is FLEET_ASSIGNED_WORKTREE's basename, else the basename of the
cwd's .claude/worktrees/<name> checkout. Contract: docs/agents/FLEET-RUNTIME.md
§ "Long-running jobs".
"""

